WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.610
- When you hear the
title, "Bride of Chucky,"

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:03.040
the first thing you're
probably gonna think of

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.150
is "Bride of Frankenstein,"

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.310
the 1935 sequel to "Frankenstein,"
starring Boris Karloff.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.760
That's the movie we see Tiffany watching

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.560
in the bathtub early on
in "Bride of Chucky."

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.580
- She's alive!

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.570
- If you haven't seen it,
there are some similarities.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.490
Primarily, the main
message of "Frankenstein"

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.590
and "Bride of Frankenstein"

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.810
which is actually just told to us

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:18.810
at verbatim in the movie.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.180
There's a character for Mary Shelley,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.690
the author of the "Frankenstein" novel,

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.340
and she explains the moral of the story

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.200
before we jump into it.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.997
- The punishment that befell a mortal man

00:00:27.997 --> 00:00:30.287
who dared to emulate God.

00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:32.660
- "Bride of Chucky"
explores similar territory.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.650
Although it has no
opening were Don Mancini

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.890
just straight up tells the
audience what the movie is about,

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.830
it tells the story of Tiffany Valentine,

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.300
who collects the pieces of the Chucky doll

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.500
and stitches them back together

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.010
to try to bring back her
ex-boyfriend, Charles Lee Ray,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.330
but ends up regretting it when
she's treated poorly by him.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.500
I'm gonna talk about the
more specific homages

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.960
that "Bride of Chucky" paid
to "Bride of Frankenstein,"

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.530
but there is another horror
movie that, ironically,

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.970
probably influenced "Bride
of Chucky" way more.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.350
To learn the significance
of Tiffany's nail file,

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.444
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:00.444 --> 00:01:03.444
(upbeat rock music)

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.890
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.100
Back in 2019, I made a series of videos

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.230
on the "Child's Play" movies,

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.350
the first three movies
in the Chucky franchise.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.570
So if you wanna watch those,

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.150
you can check out to this playlist.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.040
And if you're already
watching that playlist,

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.527
now you know why I'm suddenly
significantly less awkward.

00:01:20.527 --> 00:01:22.950
"Bride of Chucky" is a
sequel to "Child's Play 3,"

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.170
taking place no more than
a couple of months after.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.210
It would be the first movie

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.400
not to feature series
protagonist Andy Barclay,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.180
because they screwed
themselves in the third one

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.180
by recasting Andy with an older actor,

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.330
and now that actor is too old to play Andy

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.230
because the movie is set
while he's still a teen.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.120
I mean, they could go
back to the original Andy

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.480
who is now the perfect age,

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.680
but then it would clearly
be two different people.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.170
I think a lot of people
probably just wanted

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.010
to see Brad Dourif back as Chucky though,

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:46.430
and they would've gotten their wish.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.197
Let's get in to The Things You Missed.

00:01:48.197 --> 00:01:50.245
(sword zings)
(tense suspenseful music)

00:01:50.245 --> 00:01:54.070
(air whooshing)
(tense suspenseful music)

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.380
In both "Bride of Frankenstein"
and "Bride of Chucky,"

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.400
the revivals are triggered by electricity.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.130
The voodoo spell used to bring back Chucky

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.760
involves a supernatural storm cloud

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.010
issuing a strike of lightning.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.740
Then Chucky kills Tiffany by
electrocuting her in the bath

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.610
and uses the spell to transfer her soul

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:08.560
into another doll.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.540
This time Chucky is
stitched together by hand

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.970
after Tiffany retrieved the pieces

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.760
that were torn apart in
the giant spinning fan

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.140
at the end of "Child's Play 3."

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.590
This gives him a similar look
to Frankenstein's monster

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:19.800
who is famously stitched
together by his creator.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.633
In both movies,

00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:23.440
the titular couples don't
end up getting along.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.773
(classical tense music)

00:02:31.891 --> 00:02:33.542
- [Monster] Friend?

00:02:33.542 --> 00:02:36.292
(bride chuckles)

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.435
Friend?

00:02:38.435 --> 00:02:41.890
(footsteps thudding)

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.070
(bride screams)

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.010
- But as I mentioned,

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.410
I don't think "Bride of Frankenstein"

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.700
was the biggest inspiration
for the fourth Chucky movie.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.860
If you look at some of the marketing,

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.840
it becomes very clear
that Universal Pictures

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.410
was trying to capitalize on the success

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.800
of a more recent franchise,

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.670
as the official poster is a
direct parody of "Scream 2,"

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.350
and the logo with its pointy K

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.297
is basically rip off of the "Scream" logo.

00:03:00.297 --> 00:03:03.050
"Scream" took the horror
world by storm in 1996,

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.970
thanks in part to its horror genre satire

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.247
and abundant self-awareness.

00:03:06.247 --> 00:03:07.880
"Scream" is basically a slasher movie

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.250
that knows it's a slasher movie,

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.220
and "Scream 2" satirizes the cliches

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.420
of horror movie sequels.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.580
The opening scene of "Scream"
references many horror movies

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.413
that came before it

00:03:15.413 --> 00:03:17.720
in the iconic "Do you like
scary movies?" dialogue,

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.527
which includes references to "Halloween,"

00:03:19.527 --> 00:03:21.940
"Nightmare on Elm Street,"
and "Friday the 13th."

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.320
The opening scene of "Bride of Chucky"

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.750
does a very similar thing.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.010
We look inside the evidence room

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.350
at the Lockport Police Department,

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.420
where we see Michael Myers's
mask from "Halloween,"

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.370
Freddy Kruger's glove from
"Nightmare on Elm Street,"

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.550
and Jason's mask from "Friday the 13th."

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.500
This may also be Leatherface's chainsaw

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.130
from "The Texas Chainsaw Massacre."

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.830
A cop gathers up the remains of Chucky

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:39.960
and brings them to Tiffany,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.700
who takes him out with
her sharp nail file,

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.080
which has this curved tip

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.950
that makes it look like
the knife used by Ghostface

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.150
in the "Scream" movies.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.420
Additionally, there's a moment

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.010
during that opening scene of "Scream"

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.390
where the killer refers
to Casey as Blondie.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.720
- [Ghostface] Can you
handle that? Blondie?

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.050
- Chucky's bride ends
up being a blonde woman

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.220
who's soul gets transferred
into a black haired-doll,

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.820
so she bleaches the hair back to blonde

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:01.890
while listening to Blondie.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.850
The name of the Blondie song is "Call Me."

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.730
The killer in "Scream" intimidates victims

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.830
by calling them on the phone,

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.220
and Tiffany hires her neighbor

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.590
to transport the dolls in Bride

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:10.610
by calling him on the phone

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.870
so that he doesn't find out
that she's one of the dolls.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.810
Shout out to this guy for
getting a couple of horror movies

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.130
into the top comments on the
music video for "Call Me."

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.950
As I mentioned, Scream's biggest gimmick

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.430
is that it's very self-aware.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:22.090
Now, I don't want to spoil
it by showing the clip

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.120
in case there are people
that haven't seen "Scream,"

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.489
but if I did show the
clip, it would be this.

00:04:26.489 --> 00:04:27.791
(tense foreboding music)

00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:29.780
(air whooshing)

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.320
- Corn syrup.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.390
Same stuff they use for
pig's blood in "Carrie."

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.310
- So it's important to note

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.850
that the first three "Child's Play" movies

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:36.683
weren't like that,

00:04:36.683 --> 00:04:37.970
they were just like regular movies,

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:39.720
and now all the sudden after "Scream,"

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.801
Chucky has become very self-aware.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:42.660
- In fact, if it was a movie,

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:46.010
it would take three or four
sequels just to do it justice.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.040
- And there are all of these
horror movie references,

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.360
such as Chucky's head
spinning around 180 degrees

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.570
like the scene in "The Exorcist,"

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:52.950
the character Damien Blaylock

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.620
being a combination of
two characters' names

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.453
from "The Omen,"

00:04:55.453 --> 00:04:57.460
Chucky telling Tiff to turn to page 217

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.530
in the "Voodoo For Dummies" book,

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.090
which is the same as
the haunted room number

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.790
in Stephen King's novel "The Shining,"

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:04.120
Jade asking David this question...

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.490
- David, do you remember when
you were seeing Brad Barker?

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.520
- Which seems to be a
combination of Brad Dourif,

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.147
who plays Chucky and Clive
Barker who created "Hellraiser."

00:05:11.147 --> 00:05:12.610
"Hellraiser" is also referenced

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:14.440
after Chucky and Tiffany
take out Jade's uncle,

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.100
Chief Kincaid, by launching these nails

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.910
into his face using the van's airbag.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:20.400
- Why does that look so familiar?

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.520
- That would be because
he now resembles Pinhead,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.447
the iconic character in
the "Hellraiser" movies.

00:05:24.447 --> 00:05:25.320
"Hellraiser" came out

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.490
a year before Charles
Lee Ray originally died,

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:29.900
so it might've been one of
the last movies he ever saw.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.290
In fact, if we take a closer look

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.550
at this article about his death,

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.300
the newspaper reporter
includes an interview

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.840
with Mike Norris, the police
officer from "Child's Play."

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:37.780
He describes the scene

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.000
as being "like something
out of a horror movie."

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.740
There are some other
non-horror references,

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.560
like Tiffany's spider
being named Charlotte

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.290
and officer Norton referring
to Jesse as "Boogie Nights."

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.130
One of the mysteries
of the franchise so far

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.800
regards to the Haitian deity Damballa,

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.470
who Chucky calls upon
to give him the power

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.400
to transfer souls.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.570
We've heard this Damballa
chant many times before,

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.260
but this time we see it in writing

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.360
inside of Tiffany's "Voodoo
For Dummies" manual.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.820
That means that an English speaker

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.941
such as myself can properly
translate it for the first time.

00:06:02.941 --> 00:06:05.858
(thunder clapping)

00:06:08.059 --> 00:06:11.990
(tense suspenseful music)

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.607
The Damballa chant is a
French incantation meaning,

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:15.987
"To the almighty Damballa.

00:06:15.987 --> 00:06:17.497
Give me the power I beg of you.

00:06:17.497 --> 00:06:18.767
To the mercy of my soul.

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:19.600
To the point of my death.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.160
Hear me out from my condemned voice."

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.580
Damballa is a Haitian entity,
and if you're unaware,

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.590
in Haiti, the official language is French,

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.800
so that's why the incantation
has to be in French.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.660
There's actually a recurring
theme of French phrases

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.720
being used in the movie.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.390
When Damien is cringefully
trying to seduce Tiffany

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:35.223
at the beginning,

00:06:35.223 --> 00:06:37.980
he tells her about the French
saying "La Petite Mort,"

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.060
the little death, and
invites her onto the bed

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.890
to quote, unquote "die a little."

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:44.190
She asked him if he's
ready for a menage a trois,

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.460
which is French for threesome,

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.870
which is also a clue that
Chucky is actually alive,

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.440
but Damien doesn't quite get it.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.730
- What's that?

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.780
- Finally, when Tiffany
confronts the thieving couple

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.613
at the love motel,

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:56.320
she throws a bottle of
champagne called Gout de Reims

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:57.410
or Taste of Reims,

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:58.830
which is the capital of the champagne

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.550
and wine growing region in France.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.460
Now, if you would please draw
your attention to the boobs,

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.050
you'll notice that Tiffany has a tattoo

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.060
with Chucky's name on it,

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.200
and the heart is getting
stabbed by this little dagger.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.450
She actually transfers this
tattoo to her doll body

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.630
after her soul is transferred,

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.050
during the scene where she dyes her hair

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.050
and gives the doll a makeover
to look more like her.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.950
I don't know what the point
of going through all that was,

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.640
because she's planning
on transferring back

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:21.150
into a human body, like
within the next 24 hours.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.940
Seems like a lot of wasted effort.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.060
But I think the tattoo shows

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.440
that losing Chucky in the
1980s broke her heart,

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:27.810
but I also find it interesting

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.250
because in the first movie,
that's how you defeat Chucky,

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.690
Norris shoots him through the heart,

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:33.060
because his organs have turned human.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:35.200
However, Bride gives new meaning to rules

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.070
from the first movie,

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:38.530
where John Bishop told them
they had to destroy the heart.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.490
Maybe he didn't mean

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:41.070
that they had to shoot
Chucky in the heart,

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.350
because that obviously only
puts them down temporarily,

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.750
maybe he meant that they
needed to destroy this amulet,

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.000
The Heart of Damballa.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.700
I don't quite get why they feel the need

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:49.970
to retrieve the amulet though,

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.220
because Chucky never attempts

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.060
to get it in the first
three "Child's Play" movies,

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.470
and there is a later movie
where he takes over a human body

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.480
without the amulet.

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:57.450
So...

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.470
I don't know. I don't have
an answer on this one.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.820
But on the way to retrieve it,

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.980
Chucky and Tiffany cause
mayhem all around them,

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.570
taking out several police
officers and other bystanders,

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:08.110
causing their chauffeurs, the
young couple Jessie and Jade,

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:09.160
to look very guilty

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.170
as death follows them
everywhere that they go.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.420
As they drive through the night,

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.507
we hear one other song
that I wanna talk about,

00:08:14.507 --> 00:08:16.660
"See You In Hell" by Monster Magnet.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.667
This song contains the following lyrics:

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:20.337
"What time and snow couldn't bury

00:08:20.337 --> 00:08:21.727
Years of forgotten guilt.

00:08:21.727 --> 00:08:23.557
That little body's calling, rising up

00:08:23.557 --> 00:08:25.470
from under a Jersey landfill."

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.810
Well, it isn't a landfill,

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.210
but they're traveling to New Jersey

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:30.190
where the body of Charles
Lee Ray would rise up

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.190
from underground when
his skeleton is exhumed

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.480
to double-check that he's really dead

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.690
because Chucky's been leaving
Charles Lee Ray fingerprints

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.240
behind at all the crime scenes.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.157
There's also the title
of the song to consider,

00:08:39.157 --> 00:08:40.180
"See You In Hell."

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.970
Last episode, I talked
about how Chucky falling

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:43.750
into the pit in The
Devil's Lair dark ride,

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.680
symbolized him descending down into hell,

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.427
so the title foreshadows
this parting line in Bride:

00:08:49.427 --> 00:08:50.433
- [Tiffany] Goobye, Darling.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.947
I'll see you in hell.

00:08:53.947 --> 00:08:54.970
(Chucky exhales sharply)

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.900
- Chucky is able to
finish Tiffany off though,

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:59.070
so it ends up being Jesse
who shovel-yeets him

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:01.725
into his own casket, where
he starts freaking out.

00:09:01.725 --> 00:09:03.421
(dramatic music)

00:09:03.421 --> 00:09:05.860
(Chucky screaming)

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:07.110
- What's the matter, Chucky?

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.430
You act like you've never
seen a dead body before.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:11.010
The very last thing in this movie

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.260
is the explosive birth
of Chucky's offspring,

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:16.240
which leads us into the next
Chucky movie: "Seed of Chucky."

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.130
I'm not thrilled about covering that one,

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.380
but if I wanna get to Curse,

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:20.930
I'm gonna have to get through it.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.500
So, check out that video on the left

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.670
and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.110
for new horrors every week,

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.700
ring the death bell and
select All Notifications,

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.870
and I will see you in the next one.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.025
Assuming we both survive.

00:09:33.025 --> 00:09:35.692
(upbeat music)

